                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Okay game that is full of minor issues that end up ruining your experience.\n\n* Brute-forcing the puzzle usually works a lot better than trying to carefully plan ahead because there are way too many things to consider. Not my kind of puzzle, but it could be yours. Those puzzles seem nice enough if you like that style, which I don't.\n\n- Gamepad support is bad. It kinda works, except there's no pause button, and navigating the menus is awful.\n- Every time I beat a level or unlock an achievement, the games produces a Window Security pop-up trying to login to their servers. Every. Single. Time.\n- None of the options from settings actually work. You can change them, like fullscreen or volume, but there's no actual change.\n- Some optional side-puzzles make no sense at all, even for those who solved them.\n- Game is terribly flawed and seems to have been abandoned.\n\nEven if you have already purchased this, I'd say \"Don't waste your time\".",
